3,Swampy Cree - grokipedia.com,https://grokipedia.com/page/Swampy_Cree,"Swampy Cree, known to its speakers as nêhinawêwin or néhinawak, is a dialect of the Cree language within the Algonquian branch of the Algic language family, spoken primarily by the Mushkego or Swampy Cree people in subarctic regions of Canada. It is classified as an ""n-dialect,"" characterized by phonological features such as the use of /n/ in reflexive prefixes and first-person singular ...","Cree, Swampy",Algic
